#====================================================================
# Draft: clang15 -Werror turns -Wfortify-source (sscanf %Ns overflow)
#        and -Wmisleading-indentation into hard errors in upstream
#        test/build code — downgrade with -Wno-error=<class>
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-ASTRONOMY-2.1.9-CLANG15-FORTIFY-MISLEADING-INDENTATION-WERROR
trigger_tool:           clang|ctest|ctbuild|generate|sscanf|novas.c|make
phase:                  compile
error_signature:        'sscanf' may overflow; destination buffer in argument [0-9]+ has size [0-9]+, but the corresponding specifier may require size [0-9]+|misleading indentation; statement is not part of the previous 'if'|\[-Werror,-Wfortify-source\]|\[-Werror,-Wmisleading-indentation\]

severity:               2
category:               toolchain-strict-warning
match_keywords:         -Werror, -Wfortify-source, -Wmisleading-indentation, sscanf, %20s, buffer overflow, clang 15, OHOS, NOVAS, upstream tests, ctbuild, warning to error, -Wno-error

title:                  clang15/OHOS upgrades -Wfortify-source (sscanf fixed-width specifier vs buffer) and -Wmisleading-indentation to hard errors under upstream -Wall -Werror test builds; downgrade the specific classes instead of patching sources

root_cause:             Upstream test harnesses (generate/ctbuild, demotest, gravsim) compile with -Wall -Werror. The OHOS clang15 toolchain enables stricter checks than the upstream gcc environment: -Wfortify-source flags sscanf calls whose %Ns specifier can exceed the destination buffer (e.g. %20s into char[20], needing 21 for NUL), and -Wmisleading-indentation flags irregularly indented if/else blocks in legacy numerical code (e.g. NOVAS). Both are promoted by -Werror, breaking the build even though the code is correct.

affected_scope:         Any package whose upstream test/build code is compiled with -Werror on clang15 (OHOS toolchain) and contains sscanf with fixed-width specifiers or legacy indentation; verified instance - astronomy 2.1.9 ctest.c + generate/novas.c.

verification_cmd:       clang -O3 -ffp-contract=off -Wall -Werror -Wno-error=fortify-source -Wno-error=misleading-indentation -o ctest -I ../source/c/ ../source/c/astronomy.c ctest.c -lm && ./ctest all

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           downgrade-specific-warning-classes-in-test-build
rec_description:        Do not patch the upstream source. When the failure is a specific -W<class> promoted by -Werror in test-only code, append -Wno-error=<class> (not a blanket -Wno-error) to the compile line for the test harness. Prefer wrapper scripts that append the flags after -Werror so ordering cannot re-enable them. Keep the library itself compiled with strict flags; document the difference in the test report.
rec_command:            CC wrapper: exec clang "$@" -Wno-error=fortify-source -Wno-error=misleading-indentation  (invoked for ctbuild/generate builds)
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               none (test build flags only; no source patch)

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      patch-source-sscanf-buffer
fallback_description:   If the package requires -Werror to stay intact and the sscanf call is genuinely overflow-prone, fix the buffer size in a minimal portability patch (char[21] for %20s) instead of downgrading warnings.
fallback_command:       edit the sscanf destination buffer size and rebuild
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       blanket -Wno-error with no class|patch out -Werror from upstream build scripts inside the archive|#ifdef __OHOS__ guards in patches for this|disable the whole warning class for the shipped library
forbid_1_reason:        Blanket disabling hides real problems; editing upstream build scripts in the archive diverges and trips R8/PF5 (platform macro ban); the library itself must keep strict checks.
forbid_1_consequence:   Preflight rejection, non-portable patches, or weakened library build checks.

principles:             minimal-patch, real-evidence-over-assumption, upstream-fidelity, toolchain-agnostic
